  "question": {
    "text": "The half life period of a radioactive substance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math>&nbsp;days. The time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> th of its original mass to disintegrate will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math> days",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>130</mn></math> days",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn></math> days",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> days",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given half life period of a radioactive substance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>&nbsp;days.</p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mi>th</mi></math>&nbsp;of radioactive substance&nbsp;disintegrates means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mi>th</mi></math>&nbsp;remains or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;half lives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>days</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
